    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Site with Full Planning Permission in the heart of Ballydehob village.\r\n\r\nAn excellent opportunity to acquire a prime development site with full planning permission in the charming village of Ballydehob. Extending to approximately 260sqm, the site benefits from planning permission (Ref: 26/0907) for the construction of a contemporary three-bedroom detached home extending to approximately 154sqm. \r\n\r\nOccupying an elevated position with public road frontage, the approved development includes the demolition of an existing garage/store and the construction of a stylish two-storey residence with all associated site works.\r\n\r\nThe thoughtfully designed accommodation comprises a bright open-plan kitchen, dining and living area, together with a utility room and guest WC on the ground floor. Upstairs, the layout provides three generous bedrooms, including a master bedroom with en-suite, along with a modern family bathroom.\r\n\r\nBallydehob is one of West Cork's most picturesque and vibrant villages, renowned for its creative community, colourful streetscape, and spectacular coastal surroundings. Long favoured by artists, writers and nature lovers, the village offers an exceptional lifestyle with cafés, pubs, galleries and local amenities all within walking distance.\r\n\r\nThe bustling market town of Skibbereen is approximately 10 miles away, while Cork Airport can be reached in around 80 minutes by car, making this an ideal location for a permanent residence, holiday home or investment project.\r\n\r\nTitle: Freehold"
      }
